; Tutorial_0_Overview.inix -- overview

[about]
Title=0 - Overview
Intro=What bookFido is, what it gathers, and the ten walks that teach it.
Setup=Nothing to set up; this walk only listens.
Homework=List the libraries you use: Audible, Kindle, Goodreads, Bookshare, NLS. Walk three gathers them.

[step]

Say=Welcome. This is the first of ten short walks through bookFido. I am the host; the other voice is the screen reader, speaking as it would on your own computer.
Key=

[step]

Say=You know your screen reader's own keys already, and three of them are worth remembering whenever you feel lost or unsure. Insert plus Up Arrow says the line you are on again.
Key=Insert+Up Arrow
Hear=OK button

[step]

Say=Insert plus Tab says what has the focus: its name, its role, and its value or state.
Key=Insert+Tab
Hear=Audible check box, checked

[step]

Say=Insert plus T says the title of the window.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=bookFido

[step]

Say=If you set your screen reader to use Caps Lock in place of Insert, Caps Lock works the same way for all three.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=bookFido gathers every book you own or have read, from up to five libraries, into one catalog you can read, search and sort.
Key=

[step]

Say=The libraries are Audible, Kindle, Goodreads, Bookshare, and NLS, the National Library Service's talking book collection.
Key=

[step]

Say=It signs in as you in Microsoft Edge and reads the same pages you would read yourself, politely and slowly, and it sends nothing about your books anywhere.
Key=

[step]

Say=Then it fills in what the libraries leave out: publication years, publishers, descriptions, and author biographies, from Open Library and Wikipedia.
Key=

[step]

Say=The result is one combined catalog in order by title, a document for each library, a workbook, and a database you can browse in DbDo.
Key=

[step]

Say=Here are the walks. One, the dialog. Two, installing. Three, your first catalog. Four, reading it. Five, Audible's companion PDFs.
Key=

[step]

Say=Six, Goodreads shelves and reviews. Seven, NLS and Bookshare history. Eight, the catalog in DbDo and keeping it current. Nine, the conclusion, a glossary, and help.
Key=

[step]

Say=Each walk is a few minutes long and builds on the last, so they are best heard in order the first time. Walk one comes next.
Key=
